{
  "id": "trace-demo",
  "topologyId": "trace-demo",
  "title": "Measured example: from Seoul to a US server (demo data)",
  "question": "example.org",
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "narration": "You typed \"example.org\" into the address bar and pressed Enter. The browser first parses the address into a protocol (https), host (example.org), port (443) and path (/).",
      "hops": [],
      "nodeActions": [
        {
          "node": "d-browser",
          "text": "Parse URL: https://example.org:443/",
          "kind": "process"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "narration": "This site is registered for HSTS (a promise to always connect over HTTPS), so the browser changes http://example.org/ to https://example.org/ without even asking the server. No unencrypted request ever goes out.",
      "hops": [],
      "nodeActions": [
        {
          "node": "d-browser",
          "text": "HSTS: http → https (measured)",
          "kind": "rewrite"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "narration": "The browser asks the operating system, \"What is the IP address of example.org?\" Turning names into addresses is the job of the OS's DNS resolver.",
      "hops": [
        {
          "path": ["d-browser", "d-resolver"],
          "packet": {
            "protocol": "LOCAL",
            "summary": "getaddrinfo(example.org)",
            "layers": [
              {
                "name": "Function call",
                "fields": {
                  "function": "getaddrinfo",
                  "name": "example.org",
                  "request": "IPv4 and IPv6 addresses"
                },
                "sources": {
                  "function": "typical",
                  "name": "observed",
                  "request": "typical"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "nodeActions": [
        {
          "node": "d-resolver",
          "text": "Check OS DNS cache → miss, ask the DNS server",
          "kind": "lookup"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "narration": "The resolver sends a query to the DNS server 192.168.4.1 on UDP port 53. The destination IP is the DNS server, but on the first link the destination MAC is the home router.",
      "hops": [
        {
          "path": ["d-resolver", "d-stack", "d-nic", "h-router"],
          "packet": {
            "protocol": "DNS",
            "summary": "example.org A?",
            "layers": [
              {
                "name": "802.11 (Wi-Fi)",
                "fields": {
                  "Address 1 (AP)": "router's wireless MAC",
                  "Address 2 (sender)": "02:00:5e:10:00:02",
                  "Address 3 (destination)": "02:4c:a0:3d:05:0e"
                },
                "sources": {
                  "Address 1 (AP)": "typical",
                  "Address 2 (sender)": "observed",
                  "Address 3 (destination)": "observed"
                }
              },
              {
                "name": "IPv4",
                "fields": {
                  "src": "192.168.4.23",
                  "dst": "192.168.4.1",
                  "ttl": "64",
                  "protocol": "TCP (6)"
                },
                "sources": {
                  "src": "observed",
                  "dst": "observed",
                  "ttl": "typical",
                  "protocol": "typical"
                }
              },
              {
                "name": "UDP",
                "fields": {
                  "srcPort": "ephemeral port",
                  "dstPort": "53"
                },
                "sources": {
                  "srcPort": "typical",
                  "dstPort": "typical"
                }
              },
              {
                "name": "DNS",
                "fields": {
                  "question": "example.org A",
                  "id": "random 16-bit value"
                },
                "sources": {
                  "question": "observed",
                  "id": "typical"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "nodeActions": [
        {
          "node": "h-router",
          "text": "The router's DNS forwarder asks the ISP's DNS on the laptop's behalf",
          "kind": "process"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
